meta {
  name: Approve or decline (reviewer)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/promotions/{{promoteDocId}}/decide
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "approve": true,
    "note": ""
  }
}

docs {
  `approve: true` re-homes the document to the shared `promoted:org` bucket — an ownerless
  commons source, which is what makes every visibility predicate already in the codebase
  start including it with no read-path change at all. Same `doc_id`, same chunks, same
  vectors, same citations, same graph edges: a metadata flip, not a copy.

  `approve: false` leaves the document exactly where it was and records `note` as a reason
  the author can act on.

  Verify with the search request in folder `4-query` as a DIFFERENT user: empty before,
  a hit after.
}
